 "notes": "Headline combined joint-likelihood limit from Fig. 3 (total_contourplot.pdf) of the e-print: region where ALP hypothesis is disfavoured at >3 sigma vs no-ALP, from a stack of 4-5 blazars (1ES0229, VER J0521, 1ES1218+304, plus joint fit). Boundary traced as vector path (black stroke) and calibrated from axis tick labels: x=m_ALP in neV (converted to eV, 1 neV=1e-9 eV), y=g_agamma in units 10^-11 GeV^-1, both log. Curve is flat near ~2.9e-11 GeV^-1 up to ~10 neV, dips to a minimum ~2.4e-11 near 17-20 neV, then rises steeply beyond ~250 neV, consistent with the abstract statement g_agamma > ~3e-11 GeV^-1 excluded for masses up to ~200-300 neV. confidence_level=0.9973 corresponds to the paper stated >3 sigma exclusion. Not a DM search (blazar gamma-ray transparency via ALP-photon mixing), so no DM density assumption. Same curve is labelled HAWC in Fig. 4.",
